{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["The vav of <b>ונתתי</b> ['and I will give'] is like the vav of והארץ היתה תהו ובהו. And always, when the word is milraʿ with a vav, the sense is future; if mileʿel, past — except for a few instances." "<b>יבולה.</b> From כי בול הרים ישאו לו. And we do not know whether the yod is a root letter or is not a root letter, like the word יקום."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The reference is to Genesis 1:2; Ibn Ezra is drawing a phonological/syntactic analogy between the vav-prefixed forms."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:36.303801660Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}